    "causal_summary": "`cli-pi` was built to structurally mirror `cli-devin`/`cli-cursor` from the start (phase 003's skill packet, phases 005/006/008's designs), but a direct file-by-file comparison found three real gaps that had grown since: (1) `cli-pi` never gained a \"unique capabilities\" reference — both `cli-devin` (`devin-tools.md`) and `cli-cursor` (`cursor-tools.md`) have one, cataloging what makes that CLI distinctive versus its 5 siblings; (2) two of `cli-pi`'s own references (`native-skills-and-extensions.md`, `mcp-and-third-party-packages.md`) still framed several claims as \"Per Pi docs, unconfirmed\"",
